            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Enthalpy change of atomization",
            "text": "“The standard enthalpy change of atomization of an element is the enthalpy change involved when one mole of gaseous atoms is formed from the element, under standard conditions.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{H2_{(g)} -> 2H_{(g)}}\\qquad E_{\\text{H-H}} = +436\\ \\text{kJ mol}^{-1}",
            "text_alt": "H₂(g) → 2H(g)    EH–H = +436 kJ mol⁻¹"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{1/2 H2_{(g)} -> H_{(g)}}\\qquad \\Delta H^\\circ_{at} = +218\\ \\text{kJ mol}^{-1}",
            "text_alt": "½ H₂(g) → H(g)    ΔH°at = +218 kJ mol⁻¹"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
